---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { legal } from '../data/legal';

/**
 * Terms of service, governed by Australian law.
 *
 * Two constraints shape the wording:
 *
 *   * The Australian Consumer Law. Its consumer guarantees cannot be excluded,
 *     so the disclaimer and liability clauses are expressly subject to it
 *     rather than "as is" without qualification — a blanket exclusion is not
 *     merely unenforceable here, it is itself a contravention.
 *   * gate:copy. Licensing, deployment model and pricing are undecided, so
 *     the fees clause commits to notice before charging, not to a price or to
 *     the absence of one.
 *
 * The platform clause names the YouTube Terms of Service, which YouTube API
 * Services require an app's own terms to bind users to.
 */
const { entity, abn, contactPath, governingState } = legal;

const sections = [
  { id: 'agreement', title: 'This agreement' },
  { id: 'the-service', title: 'The service' },
  { id: 'accounts', title: 'Your account' },
  { id: 'your-content', title: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'connected-platforms', title: 'Connected platforms' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', title: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'fees', title: 'Fees' },
  { id: 'our-ip', title: 'Our intellectual property' },
  { id: 'consumer-law', title: 'Australian Consumer Law' },
  { id: 'liability', title: 'Liability' },
  { id: 'termination', title: 'Suspension and termination' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to these terms' },
  { id: 'law', title: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms for using the Tamtree website, waitlist and product, including connecting YouTube, Facebook, Instagram and TikTok accounts."
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="agreement">This agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {entity} (ABN {abn}) ("Tamtree", "we", "us").
    They cover this website, the waitlist, and the Tamtree product (together, "the service"). By
    using the service you agree to them. If you use it for an organisation, you agree on its behalf
    and confirm that you are allowed to.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains how we handle personal information and forms
    part of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-service">The service</h2>
  <p>
    Tamtree is an agent-first workflow orchestrator. It runs workflows you build, including steps
    that call AI models and third-party services. Tamtree is in early development. Features may
    change, be limited or be withdrawn, and access is given at our discretion. Joining the
    waitlist does not guarantee access.
  </p>
  <p>
    Workflows can produce outputs, including AI-generated content, that are wrong or unsuitable.
    You decide what a workflow does and what it publishes, and you should review outputs before
    relying on them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accounts">Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 18, or the age of majority where you live.</li>
    <li>Keep your sign-in details and API keys secure, and tell us promptly about any unauthorised use.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for what happens under your account, including the actions of workflows you run.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="your-content">Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You keep ownership of everything you put into Tamtree and everything your workflows produce
    ("your content"). You give us a limited licence to host, process, transmit and display your
    content only as needed to provide the service to you. When you tell a workflow to publish
    something, that includes sending it to the platform you chose.
  </p>
  <p>
    You confirm that you have the rights to your content and that it does not break the law or
    anyone else's rights. That includes the music, footage and likenesses in videos you upload.
  </p>

  <h2 id="connected-platforms">Connected platforms</h2>
  <p>
    You can connect accounts on other platforms, such as YouTube, Facebook, Instagram and TikTok,
    using developer apps and tokens you create yourself. When you do:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your use of each platform remains subject to that platform's own terms. By using Tamtree's
      YouTube features you agree to be bound by the{' '}
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>. The{' '}
      <a href="https://www.facebook.com/terms" rel="noopener">Meta</a>,{' '}
      <a href="https://help.instagram.com/581066165581870" rel="noopener">Instagram</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/terms-of-service" rel="noopener">TikTok</a> terms apply
      in the same way.
    </li>
    <li>
      You are responsible for the developer apps you create and for meeting their requirements,
      including any review, audit or disclosure a platform asks of you. One example is labelling
      AI-generated content where the platform requires it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Platforms decide how uploads behave. An unreviewed app's upload may be private, a draft, or
      sent to your inbox until you publish it yourself. Platforms set rate limits and can change or
      withdraw their APIs at any time. We are not responsible for a platform's actions, outages or
      changes.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where a platform cannot confirm whether an upload completed, Tamtree stops rather than retrying
      automatically, so a video is not published twice. Check the platform before running the
      workflow again.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You must not use the service to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break any law, or infringe anyone's intellectual property, privacy or other rights;</li>
    <li>publish spam, misleading content, or content that is unlawful, harmful or abusive;</li>
    <li>get around a platform's rules, limits or reviews;</li>
    <li>
      attack, probe or overload the service or its users, or try to access data that is not yours;
    </li>
    <li>
      resell or provide the service to others, or copy it to build a competing product, without our
      written permission.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="fees">Fees</h2>
  <p>
    There are currently no charges for the waitlist or for early access. If we introduce charges,
    we will tell you the price and the terms before they apply to you. Nothing will be charged
    without your agreement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="our-ip">Our intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The service, including its software, design and the Tamtree name and marks, belongs to us or
    our licensors. These terms do not give you any rights in it beyond using the service as they
    allow. If you send us feedback or suggestions, we may use them without owing you anything.
  </p>

  <h2 id="consumer-law">Australian Consumer Law</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any right or remedy you have under the
    Australian Consumer Law, or any other law, that cannot lawfully be excluded, including the
    consumer guarantees. Where the law lets us limit our liability for breaching such a guarantee,
    our liability is limited to supplying the services again, or paying the cost of having them
    supplied again.
  </p>
  <p>
    Subject to that, and to the extent the law allows, the service is provided as it is and as
    available. We do not promise that it will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that outputs will
    be accurate or suit a particular purpose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, and subject to the section above:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss of profit, revenue, data or
      goodwill;
    </li>
    <li>
      our total liability to you for all claims in connection with the service is limited to the
      amount you paid us for it in the 12 months before the claim, or AUD 100 if you paid nothing.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You are responsible for losses arising from your content, the workflows you run, and what you
    publish to connected platforms. If you use the service for a business, you agree to cover our
    reasonable costs if a third party brings a claim against us arising from those.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">Suspension and termination</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the service at any time, and ask us to close your account. We may suspend
    or end your access if you breach these terms, if your use puts the service or others at risk,
    or if we stop offering the service. Where reasonable, we will give you notice and a chance to
    export your content first. Sections that by their nature should continue, such as those on
    ownership, liability and governing law, survive termination.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the service develops. We will change the date at the top of this
    page. If a change materially affects you, we will tell you by email at least 14 days before it
    takes effect. If you keep using the service after that, you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {governingState}, Australia. You and we submit to the
    non-exclusive jurisdiction of its courts and of the federal courts of Australia.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Send questions about these terms, and legal notices, through our{' '}
    <a href={`${contactPath}?topic=legal`}>contact page</a>, choosing <strong>Legal notice</strong>.
  </p>
</Legal>
